{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/349582-powerstat-for-slashers","id":349582,"title":"Powerstat for Slashers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-24T22:50:34-08:00","id":349582,"title":"Powerstat for Slashers?","content":"I was thinking that it would be cool if Slashers had their own Powerstat, called &quot;Killer Instinct&quot; or something like that. It would have all the benefits of Conviction (World Of Darkness: Mirrors, page 32), but your Resistance would be equal to your Killer Instinct. Also, you can raise your Attributes/Skills past 5, as long as your Killer Instinct is 6 or higher and said Attributes/Skills are part of your Undertaking. Drawback: having high Killer Instinct makes it harder to resist Derangements or Derangement-like Conditions. You take a penalty equal to Killer Instinct/2 round down. This does not stack with Frailties. Lastly, it allows you to store and spend more willpower points per turn than usual for the purposes of Dread Powers and Talents (Hunter: The Vigil - Mortal Remains, page 164).<br /> <br /> What are your thoughts about this idea? Cool? Unnecessary? In need of reworking?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T23:13:39-08:00","id":349613,"title":"","content":"Functional, but unnecessary. Slashers are Hunter antagonists. They're dangerous enough to Hunters without it. It might work if you wanted to bring them as antagonists in another game, but most of them have antagonists within their own structures that already fill this niche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T01:09:23-08:00","id":349695,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> I think it would be simpler, and more genre appropriate, to adapt the Atrocity rules from Danse Macabre.<br /> <br /> Slashers gain a permanent atrocity rating equal 10 minus humanity, up to five, the atrocity rating is added to all dice pools, but any successes on the atrocity dice will result in more chaos and destruction in the slasher's life.<br /> <br /> So as slashers fall to depravity, they become capable of more impressive feats of strength and stamina, athletics, stealth, all the things that slashers are often superhuman in while in the movies. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T01:40:39-08:00","id":349698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/349582-powerstat-for-slashers?p=349695#post349695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> I think it would be simpler, and more genre appropriate, to adapt the Atrocity rules from Danse Macabre.<br /> <br /> Slashers gain a permanent atrocity rating equal 10 minus humanity, up to five, the atrocity rating is added to all dice pools, but any successes on the atrocity dice will result in more chaos and destruction in the slasher's life.<br /> <br /> So as slashers fall to depravity, they become capable of more impressive feats of strength and stamina, athletics, stealth, all the things that slashers are often superhuman in while in the movies. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>But Slashers start with their Morality stat at 4 to 0. Even &quot;good&quot; Slashers would start with maximum Atrocity this way. I see two ways to go about this:<br /> <br /> 1) Permanent Atrocity is equal to 6 - Morality (or whatever you're using).<br /> 2) Slashers can start with Morality at 7 like normal characters. Permanent Atrocity equals 10 - Morality and can go up to 10, thus capping at Morality 0. However, your Permanent Atrocity is not added to all rolls. Instead, it is a pool of dice you can acess whenever you want, and replenishes every scene. You can only boost a single roll by +5, tops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T07:20:26-08:00","id":350648,"title":"","content":"I second that it's not that necessary. Slasher are dangerous enough as they are as Hunter antagonists, and you can build them appropriately to be a legitimate threat towards other supernaturals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T18:41:03-08:00","id":351162,"title":"","content":"On the lower end, I agree with those folks who say it's pretty well unnecessary. Killers like Hannibal Lecter or Norman Bates don't usually have anything interesting going on mechanically other than their Undertaking benefit or maaaaybe the occasional 6 in a stat or supernatural merit - they're functionally normal human beings, just...twisted.<br /> <br /> On the more supernatural side of Slashers - beings like Freddy Krueger, Jason, etc. - the idea becomes a lot more viable to me, though at that point as much as I like Slashers I would probably just ditch the Undertakings thing and stat them up as monsters whole cloth, so that works out for me in any case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}